    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><em>Category: Unseen Gods</em></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">Primarily Practiced in: Bahljet, Weissel, Saljund, Jelwyn, Mann, South Rodda</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\">Espirian Domains: The Heavens (Taranthara, Asphalus)</em></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Kirahi is the sister of Krahi. She represents growth and youth. Her prominent qualities include knowledge and practice, where saplings begin to touch and feel the world, letting themselves take shape.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Title</strong> </span><span>The Second Petal</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\">Edicts </strong>Seeking knowledge, practicing a craft, honing physical abilities</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:normal\">Anathema </strong>Neglecting discipline, being slothful</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Areas of Concern</strong> Growth, Exploration, Creativity</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Religious Symbol</strong> A two-leaf sprout upon a sun</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Animal</strong> Hummingbird</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><strong>Sacred Colors</strong> green and yellow</span></p>"
